@lesson projects-m01-l07 | Expense Tracker | 45
## Learning objectives
- Build a complete expense tracker
- Practise architecture, state and testing

## Expense Tracker
Track expenses by category with totals and a simple chart.

## Dependencies
- intl
- sqflite

## Steps
1. Expense model in cents
2. Add expense form with validation
3. Group totals by category
4. Show a bar chart with CustomPainter

```dart
class Expense { Expense(this.cents, this.category); final int cents; final String category; }
Map<String, int> totals(List<Expense> list) {
  final m = <String, int>{};
  for (final e in list) { m[e.category] = (m[e.category] ?? 0) + e.cents; }
  return m;
}
```

## Testing
Write a unit test for the core logic and a widget test that taps the main action and checks the result.

## Summary
- You built a working expense tracker.
- Extend it with your own features.

